    "question": "The graph of $y = g(x)$ has domain $-1 \\le x \\le 3$ and passes through the points $(-1, 2)$, $(0, -1)$ and $(3, 4)$.\nThe graph of $y = g(x - 4) - 2$ is drawn. Write down the coordinates of the images of these three points, in the same order.",
    "level": "higher",
    "marks": 10,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Horizontal shift: g(x \u2212 4) moves the graph right 4",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "Replacing $x$ by $x - 4$ shifts every point 4 units right, so $(x, y)$ becomes $(x + 4, y)$."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Find the new domain",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "$g$ needs its input between $-1$ and $3$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "-1 \\le x - 4 &\\le 3",
         "sym": "And(-1 <= x - 4, x - 4 <= 3)",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "3 \\le x &\\le 7",
         "sym": "And(3 <= x, x <= 7)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Vertical shift: subtracting 2 moves the graph down 2",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "Every point then drops 2 units, so $(x, y)$ becomes $(x + 4, y - 2)$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "(-1, 2) &\\to (3, 0)",
         "sym": "[-1 + 4, 2 - 2]",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "(0, -1) &\\to (4, -3)",
         "sym": "[0 + 4, -1 - 2]",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "(3, 4) &\\to (7, 2)",
         "sym": "[3 + 4, 4 - 2]",
         "new": true
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "(3, 0),\\ (4, -3),\\ (7, 2)"
    },
    "finalSym": "[(3, 0), (4, -3), (7, 2)]",
    "answerSym": "[(-1 + 4, 2 - 2), (0 + 4, -1 - 2), (3 + 4, 4 - 2)]"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "skill": "geo-cor1",
  "problems": [
   {
    "question": "$ABCD$ is a parallelogram with diagonal $[AC]$.\n$|AB| = 3x - 4$ and $|CD| = x + 8$.\nFind $|CD|$.",
    "level": "higher",
    "marks": 10,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Use Corollary 1",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "The diagonal $[AC]$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles, $ABC$ and $CDA$, with $B$ matching $D$ and $A$ matching $C$."
        },
        {
         "text": "So the matching sides $[AB]$ and $[CD]$ are equal."
        },
        {
         "tex": "3x - 4 &= x + 8",
         "sym": "Eq(3*x - 4, x + 8)",
         "new": true
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Solve for $x$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "2x &= 12",
         "sym": "Eq(2*x, 12)"
        },
        {
         "tex": "x &= 6",
         "sym": "Eq(x, 6)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Find $|CD|$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "|CD| &= 6 + 8",
         "sym": "6 + 8",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 14",
         "sym": "14"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "14"
    },
    "finalSym": "14",
    "answerSym": "(8 + 4)/(3 - 1) + 8"
   }
  ]
 }
